# The SPA rewrite, and the thing that makes clean URLs possible at all.
#
# WI-29a chose HashRouter because no host was committed to this repository, and a
# BrowserRouter without this line means a refresh on /fields returns a 404 — which reads
# to the owner as the app being broken rather than as a missing config file. Netlify is
# now that host, so this line is the promise the router is relying on. Deleting it does
# not break navigation from inside the app; it breaks refresh, deep links and bookmarks,
# which is a far quieter failure.
#
# Netlify serves a real file first and only falls through to this rule when nothing
# matches, so /assets/index-abc123.js is still served as itself.
#
# This file lives in public/ rather than in netlify.toml on purpose: Vite copies it
# verbatim into dist/, so the rule ships inside the deployed artifact whoever built it.

/*    /index.html    200
